    {
      "id": "UgzpQ1K57bhQ7hWrb614AaABAg",
      "author": "@momogunsabah",
      "authorImage": "https://yt3.ggpht.com/SHyLyRzNQn-7I_pqP29bxOJ1Tje4BSgEdgFMtJIDl_C49D-zY9SxcsPmR-uOLo5_lOjHMy5pRw=s48-c-k-c0x00ffffff-no-rj",
      "text": "On August 26, 2026, a catastrophic glacier collapse and debris avalanche near the Langtang Lirung mountain peak triggered unprecedented flash floods along the Nepal-China border. \r\n\r\nThe initial impact in Langtang National Park was so immense that it generated seismic energy equivalent to a 5.2 magnitude earthquake.The disaster has primarily devastated the Rasuwa and Nuwakot districts within Nepal's Bagmati Province, as well as parts of Gyirong County in the Tibet Autonomous Region of China.\r\n\r\nKey Details of the Disaster\r\nHumanitarian Impact: As of early September 2026, the combined death toll has surpassed 1,270 people, with over 4,700 individuals still missing. Emergency crews are desperately working around the clock to locate survivors, including workers trapped deep inside heavily damaged hydropower tunnels.\r\n\r\nWidespread Destruction: A massive torrent of mud, boulders, and water surged over 100 kilometers downstream along the Trishuli River corridor. It completely buried villages, swallowed critical highways, destroyed the vital Gyirong Port checkpoint on the border, and knocked out hundreds of megawatts of Nepal’s national electrical grid. Financial damages in Nepal alone have already climbed beyond 200 billion rupees ($1.3 billion USD).\r\n\r\nEarly Warning Shortfalls: While official government SMS warning systems largely failed or arrived too late, localized, informal word-of-mouth warnings and community-based networks ultimately saved thousands of lives by prompting immediate higher-ground evacuations.\r\n\r\nThe risk of secondary disaster remains dangerously high, as temporary lakes formed by landslide debris threaten to burst their banks and trigger further flooding downstream",
      "likeCount": 0,
      "publishedAt": "2026-09-03T14:03:57Z",
      "replyCount": 0,
      "replies": []
